In quirks and limited-quirks mode, Ladybird now counts a block
ellipsis as neither text nor line height on its line, unless it
displaced all of the line’s content. Blink lays out a line whose
content the ellipsis displaced in its kLineClampDisplacedEllipsis mode,
in LogicalLineBuilder::CreateLine(), which takes the strut of the line
box in any mode. That’s from reading the source. Chrome 157.0.8103.79,
Firefox 151.0, and Playwright’s WebKit 26.5 ran the cases of the test
added here, and agree on all three; Ladybird gives what they give.
